00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,809
Swap hydrogen for deuterium in a
hydrogen-bonded crystal and, in our

2
00:00:04,829 --> 00:00:09,851
calculations, it leans toward the
polymorph with the shorter O-H bonds.

3
00:00:09,871 --> 00:00:15,249
Three machine-learned potentials get this
sign in 185 of 212 cases where the

4
00:00:15,269 --> 00:00:20,930
hydrogen bonds are moderate or strong, and
the rule says where it stops working.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:27,307
Polymorph energy gaps are smaller than any
machine-learned potential's error.

6
00:00:27,327 --> 00:00:34,209
So we compute only the isotope difference.
Force constants do not depend on mass, so

7
00:00:34,229 --> 00:00:40,700
one phonon calculation gives both hydrogen
and deuterium free energies, and the

8
00:00:40,720 --> 00:00:45,547
static gap cancels.
Three universal potentials do the work;

9
00:00:45,567 --> 00:00:47,930
SevenNet only votes on signs.

10
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:53,427
We screened 220 polymorph pairs.
The isotope free-energy difference follows

11
00:00:53,447 --> 00:00:59,310
the change in mean O-H length, 0.11 to
0.13 meV per hydrogen per thousandth of an

12
00:00:59,330 --> 00:01:03,086
angstrom.
The O-H stretch drives it, and bending and

13
00:01:03,106 --> 00:01:07,807
libration cancel about half.
Where hydrogen bonds are moderate or

14
00:01:07,827 --> 00:01:13,762
strong, deuteration favours the shorter
O-H bonds in 185 of 212 model evaluations.

15
00:01:13,782 --> 00:01:17,321
A baseline that always guesses one sign
gets 131.

16
00:01:17,341 --> 00:01:23,349
Counted per pair, 74 are right and 10 are
wrong, and all 10 wrong pairs contain the

17
00:01:23,369 --> 00:01:28,869
same aluminium hydroxide structure, where
bending and libration outweigh the

18
00:01:28,889 --> 00:01:32,355
stretch.
With weak hydrogen bonds it fails, 2 of

19
00:01:32,375 --> 00:01:35,477
20.
We chose that boundary after seeing the

20
00:01:35,497 --> 00:01:36,930
data, and we say so.

21
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,242
Is this a shared model bias? Their O-H
stretch frequencies follow the slope

22
00:01:43,262 --> 00:01:49,587
measured from real mineral spectra, for O
to O distances between 2.5 and 2.8

23
00:01:49,607 --> 00:01:53,761
angstrom.
That checks the main ingredient, not the

24
00:01:53,781 --> 00:01:54,930
